      {
        "id": 158513,
        "name": "Belle Sorciere",
        "username": "Belle_Sorciere",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/belle_sorciere/{size}/1982_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-05T23:04:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It'd be risky and if I were GtG, I wouldn't allow it. &nbsp;They'd run the risk of bad fan content being a new person's first exposure to the game and turning them off it entirely. &nbsp;Safer to make the only stuff consumers can get be official stuff.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It looks like this is going to be a thing for more than just GtG. RTC already sells several fan-made cards for Pathfinder, at least, and probably not just Pathfinder.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
