      {
        "id": 158514,
        "name": "skoticus",
        "username": "skoticus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skoticus/{size}/1964_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-06T21:51:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It'd be risky and if I were GtG, I wouldn't allow it. &nbsp;They'd run the risk of bad fan content being a new person's first exposure to the game and turning them off it entirely. &nbsp;Safer to make the only stuff consumers can get be official stuff.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I think we can trust fans and gamers more than that. People will know if they are playing the game or a fan expansion. And really, how many people introducing this to others will start with, or at least not state the difference, between the canon and Tosx's decks? I've played plenty of fan expansions of games throughout the years, but it has never been my first go into the game. And anyone stumbling onto the DTC games will still know it's a fan expansion, not the real thing.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Also, in this case, there's nothing to worry about. Tosx's decks are on par with the rest of the game. And thematically, has some of my favorites. It will lead people TO the base games, not away.</p>",
